has drawn in more than =C2=A317,000. Darvill says: =E2=80=9CWe=E2=80=99re d=
oing it because we want to raise awareness of Parkinson=E2=80=99s in Canada=
 and help those out there with Parkinson=E2=80=99s. We=E2=80=99re trying to=
 showcase sort of what we do, to try to reach more people.

=E2=80=9CWe=E2=80=99re going to play two American teams when we=E2=80=99re =
out there, an over-40s team and over-60s all women=E2=80=99s walking footba=
ll team [non-disabled], and then we=E2=80=99re going to play some men=E2=80=
=99s teams as well. We=E2=80=99re running a Parkinson=E2=80=99s fundraising=
 day too, where we will run the session ourselves, we=E2=80=99ll put on the=
 coaching drills and have a bit of fun to try to get as many people in Cana=
da interested.=E2=80=9D

For Darvill, it is a mission with a deeply personal motivation, with her ow=
n gratitude to walking football for how it is helping her dad continuing to=
 drive her to help others with the condition.

